      "problem": "Solve the equation $3p-7 =20.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $7$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n    \t\t3p-7 &=20\\\n\t\t3p-7+7 &=20+7 \\\n                3p + 0 &= 27 \\\n\t\t3p &=27\n\t}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3p &=27 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{3p}{3} &=\\dfrac{27}{3} \\[5pt]  \n\t\t\\dfrac{\\cancel{3}p}{\\cancel{3}} &= 9 \\[5pt]  \n\t\tp &=9\n\t}\n$$",
